# promise: #774
# A download from a link shows only Cra's download flight (Arc's), and Chromium puts no window of
# its own on screen away from Cra's windows (#774). Chromium threw its own download arrow at the
# download button of a toolbar nobody sees, from a popup window that came up in the primary
# display's corner before its first frame moved it. With Cra on a second display and another app
# full screen on the primary one, that window switched the primary display to a desktop on every
# download. `chrome` counts the windows of Chromium's views ordered onto the screen, `chrome-away`
# the ones that came up off every Cra window, `last-away` the last of those (class@x,y,wxh). The
# Spaces themselves take two displays: docs/release-checklist.md.
home
budget rss=600 stalls50=5
cra://open?url=file://${FIXTURES}/Pages/downloads.html
expect-log loaded file:
wait 1
cra://debug?pageWindows=before
expect-log page windows before: .* chrome-away=0 last-away=none

# A click on a link that downloads, as the page's user would.
cra://debug?cdp=Input.dispatchMouseEvent&params={"type":"mousePressed","x":36,"y":56,"button":"left","clickCount":1}
cra://debug?cdp=Input.dispatchMouseEvent&params={"type":"mouseReleased","x":36,"y":56,"button":"left","clickCount":1}
expect-log Download finished from a data: address
wait 2
cra://debug?pageWindows=download
expect-log page windows download: .* chrome-away=0 last-away=none
